# Frontend Conventions

## Auth & Utilities

- **Always** `authFetch` from `utils/authFetch.js` for API calls — never native `fetch`
- JWT: `checkTokenExpiration()` refreshes access via refresh token; on failure clears `localStorage` and redirects to login. Checks run on `PrivateRoute` page load, before each `authFetch`, and on global `keydown`/`click` (debounced in `App.jsx`)
- Prefer existing utils: `formatDate.js` (`MMM dd, YYYY`), `formatTime.js` (`formatTime` / `parseTime12hr`), `DayOfWeek.jsx`, `Tooltip.jsx`, `phone/PhoneDisplay.jsx`
- Reuse link/label components: `OrganizationLink`, `ContactLink`, `SessionLink`, `ClassLabel`
- Feature folders under `frontend/src/[feature]/` with List / Detail / Create / Edit / Link as needed
- Styling: Bootstrap + `custom.css` (and feature CSS as needed)

## Display

- Dates: `MMM dd, YYYY` · Times: 12-hour with AM/PM (backend stores 24hr)
- Days of week: always `DayOfWeek` widget — never ad-hoc day badges
- Breadcrumbs: names/identifiers, **not** numeric IDs
- Link classes: `.clickable-text` (blue on hover, no underline); `.plain-link` (black, no hover); `.active-name` (blue, no hover — for parent-driven hover activation on a field)

## Lists & Clickable Rows

- Tables with client-side sort (▲ ▼) and clear columns
- Org-scoped lists (locations, contacts, etc.): read `organization` from the URL query string and pass it to the API; offer an org filter dropdown when useful
- Clickable rows: `.clickable-row`, `tabIndex={0}`, Enter/Space → navigate; `.reactive-link-cell` / `.reactive-link-text` on cells/text
- Per-field hover links (e.g. Locations tables): hover activates only that field via `.plain-link` / `.active-name`, not the whole row

## Cards

```jsx
<div className="card shadow-sm border-primary mb-4">
  <div className="card-header bg-dark text-white d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
    <h4 className="mb-0">Title</h4>
    {/* actions */}
  </div>
  <div className="card-body">{/* ... */}</div>
</div>
```

## Fetch Pattern

`loading` / `error` / `data` state; `authFetch`; show Loading and `alert alert-danger` for errors. Forms: disable submit while saving; navigate on success.
